{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536486-ideas-for-an-atypical-character","id":1536486,"title":"Ideas for an atypical character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-28T23:44:27-07:00","id":1536486,"title":"Ideas for an atypical character","content":"Hello all.<br /> <br /> I am thinking of writing a character for Mage (maybe a Marauder, not sure if they would fit outside of that theme, but if so an Orphan?) that is rather atypical. The idea is a mage in a modern is cartoonist, has an odd religous belief called &quot;toonism&quot; and worships several major cartoon characters like Bugs Bunny, Popeye, etc. He uses spirit sphere to interact with them in the High Umbra and visit the &quot;Television Realm&quot; where ToonTown is located. His goal is to ultimately spread their influence and power across his town to counter the influence of the numerous other groups in our game, like Pentex, Vampires, banes, etc. How do you imagine other splats interacting with this character? How could I keep this kind of character &quot;serious&quot; enough to be taken seriously, but also whimsical enough to fit theme?<br /> <br /> What spheres should I prioritize at the start?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T12:44:01-07:00","id":1536522,"title":"","content":"As described this character is a Marauder, and the worse type of them, one that ridicules mental health issues.<br /> <br /> I'll assume that you want in good faith make a serious character out of this and give some ideas.<br /> <br /> Back down from the idea of worshipping cartoon characters and tweak it into loving cartoons as a medium and artistic expression. Think about what this character finds so appealing about cartoons and what life lessons they take from them.<br /> <br /> Once you have this, we can explore Spheres. If you keep the worshipping idea, I won't engage this further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T02:58:48-07:00","id":1536613,"title":"","content":"You are going to struggle to make a character like that not come off as a joke, and handled poorly it could be seen as a caricature of hyper obsessive behaviour frequently attributed with autism.<br /> <br /> I would recommended going in one of two directions<br /> <br /> 1. Put some more substance in to them. Rather than focus them on cartoons, perhaps they believe that illustrations in general are sentient beings, and to draw is to create literal worlds. Every illustration therefore has a life beyond the artist and can act independently. A good marauder concept would be to extend this to its logical extreme. In this case all illustrations come alive around them, and they can create worlds simply by drawing them. Cartoons on TV may also speak and act beyond their usual scripted limits.<br /> <br /> 2. Go the opposite route, make them a marauder who believes they are a cartoon character. This allows you to make them more like The Mask, or living in a world like Who Framed Roger Rabbit. You can still make a character like this deep and serious by considering what would drive someone to such a transformation, and put that front and centre to what they do with this power. Perhaps they latch on to toon logic as a power fantasy and use that to get back at all the people who stepped on them (again like The Mask). Perhaps they are more like The Joker where a series of bad events brought them to the edge of sanity and they simply latched on to what little shred of humanity they had left, humour, but humour void of joy, replaced instead with cruelty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T09:17:04-07:00","id":1536625,"title":"","content":"Actually, you might consider playing it straight. <br /> <br /> He is <i>not </i>a Marauder. He is <i>not </i>particularly prone to Madness, and doesn't even have any particular mental defects. There aren't any hobgoblins popping up around him like Harvey the Rabbit; and he doesn't get stuck in (or manifest) any Paradox Realms. He has to go to Toon Town in order to meet toons; and any toons encountered outside of Toon Town are only there because he facilitated their departure. <br /> <br /> Toon Town is real, as are its inhabitants. The only thing I'm debating is where it is located: is it in a \u201cTelevision Realm\u201d in the Astral Umbra, as you suggested, or is it hiding in a corner of the Digital Web that corresponds to television the way that most of the Digital Web corresponds with computers? That is, should he be using Spirit to access it, or Correspondence? Are the toons spirits, or digital entities? <br /> <br /> For dark whimsy, take inspiration from Alice in Wonderland or the Wizard of Oz; or perhaps <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cool_World\" target=\"_blank\">Cool World</a>, if you're looking for a Toon Town that's a bit off-kilter. Cartoons don't have to be kid_safe, and some of the best ones aren't; and in the World of Darkness, that's arguably even more true. <br /> <br /> You could also look at Changeling: the Dreaming for inspiration about how to get the tone right: chimera in the Dreaming can be whimsical, dark, or both. Heck, Toon Town might even be located in the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T12:45:20-07:00","id":1536633,"title":"","content":"If it is in the Digital Web, I don't think it even needs to be linked to TV, anymore. Most cartoon content, even classics, is readily available through the internet in several ways.<br /> <br /> A Mage that interacts with the Dreaming would be a very interesting option, but then they run the actual risk of becoming more embroiled with Changeling society than Mages (to whom he still comes out as in Silence anyways).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T18:35:55-07:00","id":1536655,"title":"","content":"There is a type of creature in C:tD that is a living embodiment of fictional characters, mythic beings, folkloric figures. Picture a group of these, connected to cartoons, trying to become Changelings. The older rituals that allowed the incarnation of fae spirits in human bodies don't really connect to these Toon based spirits. The Toon Mage might be allied with these spirits and seeking their incarnation to change the paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T13:02:09-07:00","id":1538012,"title":"","content":"Did you really necroed this thread just to shitpost on me?<br /> <br /> The OP literally asked for advice in making this character serious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}